 do spaced repetition  but if I have one hour a day I have to  decide am I going to be reviewing my  flashcards or am I going to be reading  or listening and so forth so to my mind  a because I don't enjoy them that much  and be because I don't think they're  necessarily that much more effective  than the enjoyable task of reading and  listening I don't do a lot of it I do  some of it and I will tell you how I do  it all right and I should point out that  because in my learning at length I very  quickly create a lot of links I've got  thousands of words links created that I  want to learn that if I were to have you  know a major effort in reviewing  flashcards even in a very you know  sophisticated spaced repetition system  that would very quickly eat up all the  time that I have available for language  learning I would find that not enjoyable  and I would not continue so what I do is  when I learn a link and and I for my  most recent languages I've been using  the many stories which in themselves  have a lot of repetition and they are  high frequency verbs then as I turn the  page of late I review so I use the  activities that we have a link and don't  forget that you can set them you because  there are five activities so there is  flashcards reverse flash cards fill in  the blanks multiple-choice and dictation  and they all have different uses  dictation was very useful for me to get  used to the Arabic writing system and  the Greek writing system but there are  times when I don't want to do dictation  I just want to review them I want the  the review for me after each page of  is an opportunity to have some  concentrated exposure to the words that  I still don't understand which I have  saved as links right so I do that right  after having read a text I will also  sometimes go to a lesson where I know  most of the words there might only be 10  or 15 words or phrases in there that I  feel I'm still struggling with rather  than reading through the whole lesson I  will simply review those words those  yellow links in our review activities  and then go away listen again so there  are many different ways that you can use  these review activities to me the review  activities are a form of concentrated  exposure so therefore I don't in my  settings for example my my link  flashcards I have all the information on  the front of the flashcard I don't want  to have to scratch my brain to try to  remember I don't think that personally I  find that that is a waste of time I  would far rather be given the meaning  all up front and it's just concentrated  reviewed now in terms of concentrated  review there are things that you can do  to enhance that activity for example  using tags so if I have trouble with  verbs of motion and Russian then I will  tag verbs of motion when I see them and  then in the vocabulary section I can  review all of the words that I tagged  for verbs of motion or if it's you know  verbs in Spanish or subjunctive or  whatever I choose to tag for then I can  have a concentrated exposure to those  words and don't forget too that with  each word you say you get example  sentences so and I find these very  useful and we now have text-to-speech  for those so that the idea to get some  concentrated exposure to things that you  have trouble remembering that's how I  use my review activity so and and of  course the fact that particularly with  the many stories in the early stages of  my learning and perhaps later on when I  want to  certain basic structures the many  stories themselves have a lot of  repetition they're a form of review so  that I wanted to share with you how I  use these activities I sometimes go to  the vocabulary section and I can look at  the srs tag or I you know tab or I can  look up it tagged some kind that I have  chosen and then have this concentrated  review until I get tired of doing it  because I can only do that for 15  minutes or so and then I lose interest  so you know I think the review is an  important part of learning a language  because it enables us to to get exposure  to content in a different way  it has the advantage to that sometimes  we're tired of reading and listening and  we want to do something else so the  review is kind of a thing that you can  do that doesn't require a lot of thought  and so it just enables us to cover some  of the same ground in a slightly  different way so I would encourage you  to do the review and to do it in the way  that suits your personal preferences and  see what works for you and it is a  feature we have an ink and make sure you  take and try to take full advantage of  it so thank you for listening and keep  on with your 90 day challenge
 

